odel. It is therefore outside primary-model screening.","evidence_snippet":"“This review systematically synthesizes research progress ... through 181 systematic reviews”"},{"record_id":"rec_000005","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"ACSCeND is a scRNA-seq and bulk RNA-seq classification/deconvolution framework. No text or language component is described in the abstract.","evidence_snippet":"“a unified, machine learning–based framework ... scRNA-seq ... and ... bulk RNA sequencing data”"},{"record_id":"rec_000006","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"DeepExoMir uses frozen RiNALMo RNA-language-model embeddings together with biologically informed features, so the language model is an external feature source rather than the core candidate model. The abstract frames this as a target-prioritization pipeline, not a substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“integrating frozen RiNALMo RNA language model embeddings with biologically informed features”"},{"record_id":"rec_000007","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper develops an integrated transcriptomic/metabolomic deep-learning framework for mechanism analysis. No text/language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“combining transcriptomic and metabolomic profiling with deep learning”"},{"record_id":"rec_000008","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This paper presents an evaluation framework and benchmark-style analyses of existing single-cell foundation models rather than a new candidate model. That makes it a resource/evaluation paper for screening purposes.","evidence_snippet":"“We present an evaluation framework comprising thirty-seven analyses and 153 statistical tests”"}]}
